{ PreTrainedConfig

  → https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/blob/3322f226a02c5c3a3c1a3f0f4a3c9cee50789f6d/src/transformers/configuration_utils.py#L299[`PreTrainedConfig`] is the base class that implements methods for loading and saving configurations.

  Class attributes which are overridden in derived classes:
  table { lll
    ~attribute~ ☰ ~type~ ☰
    `model_type` ☰ `str` ☰
    `attribute_map` ☰ `dict[str, str]` ☰ maps model specific attribute names to the standardized naming of attributes.
    `base_model_tp_plan` ☰ `dict[str, Any]` ☰  maps sub-modules FQNs of a base model to a tensor parallel plan applied to the sub-module when `model.tensor_parallel` is called.
    `base_model_fsdp_plan` ☰ `dict[Any, str]` ☰ maps sub-modules of a base model to an FSDP2 sharding strategy (e.g. `"free_full_weight"` / `"keep_full_weight"`). Keys can be wildcard module paths (e.g. `"layers.*"`) or tuples of paths (grouped into a single `fully_shard` call).
    `base_model_pp_plan` ☰ `dict[str, tuple[list[str]]]` ☰ maps child-modules of a base model to a pipeline parallel plan that enables users to place the child-module on the appropriate device.
  table }


  Common attributes in derived classes include
    • `hidden_size`
    • `num_attention_heads`
    • `num_hidden_layers`
    • `vocab_size` (Text models only)

  An example of a class that inherits from `PreTrainedConfig` is → https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/blob/3322f226a02c5c3a3c1a3f0f4a3c9cee50789f6d/src/transformers/models/qwen2/configuration_qwen2.py#L25[`Qwen2Config`].

code {
from transformers import AutoConfig

model_id = 'Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct' # 'google-bert/bert-base-uncased'

cfg = AutoConfig.from_pretrained(model_id)
print(type(cfg))

print(f'model_type:          {cfg.model_type}')
print(f'hidden_size:         {cfg.hidden_size}')
print(f'num_attention_heads: {cfg.num_attention_heads}')
